PP; initiation_type mapping.", "observed_verdict": "artifact_found"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-054", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-054: PUTBACK suppression mechanism: fatigue vs value", "score": 0.29, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_related_family (record_link_extends) FAM:SF-APPA-054", "request matches RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY (0.19); FAM:SF-APPA-054 auto_has_risk RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "PUTBACK suppression mechanism: fatigue vs value", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "PUTBACK suppresses the next star possession via fatigue (stronger in H2 and Q4), while PUTBACK itself remains high-value.", "observed_result": "H1 delta -0.038 vs H2 -0.130 (22 stars, 3.4x). Q1 -0.009 vs Q4 -0.289 (11 stars; Q4 pooled n=34). PUTBACK H2 1.528 vs 1.217 (+0.311) n=8,614 vs 474,564. After opp PUTBACK offense 1.097 vs 1.210 (d=-0.113) n=15,898.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Q4 PUTBACK is sparse (34 pooled poss at n>=30; Mitchell n=34 drives the Q4 cell) even though the H2 vs H1 and aftershock tests are larger.", "observed_verdict": "supported"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:insufficient_exposure"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-050"}]}], "n_results": 4}

